  "actualProductionChange": [
    "Public original cookie.setWebCookie/getBaseUrl/splitNotBlank calls same Host with same owner/task/absolute deadline; native uses existing default WK cookie store only and removes sessions before ordered platform setters.",
    "Original removeCookie completes DB/cache first, then same WK store expires root-path names at exact getDomain/getSubDomain targets. Errors/cancellation retain completed DB/cache and conservative native-issued facts.",
    "Original clear uses exact CookieDao SQL literal ASCII-pipe subset; same actor exact-key bounded process CacheManager view survives new RuntimeSession/Host grants, while fresh native owner/file reload sees deleted DB rows absent.",
    "Per-operation WK child tasks are cancelled on task cancellation, source revision rebinding and revoke; continuation ownership gates prevent late callbacks from advancing or publishing for later grants. This is not a global foreign-writer CAS.",
    "Issued native effects are recorded before mutation IPC may escape, including completion-not-returned timeout, forwarded in native success/error metadata and persisted only as task-local control facts before JVM cancellation guards.",
    "Cookie planning/array traversal executes in nonisolated async worker with perf span; only WK calls hop MainActor, no Main semaphore/queue wait or new WKWebView."
  ],
  "timeoutAdmissionFix": {
    "confirmedGap": "Native timeout could snapshot unsealed facts after cancelling its task while a not-yet-cancelled old Host child was between validation and installing its handler, allowing later first WK IPC with no fact in escaped timeout response.",
    "implementation": "Same request-local recorder lock now closes registrations before timeout response. Before any actual mutation IPC, continuation gate calls throwing admission; denied sealed request throws Cancellation without issuing. Cookie file operations likewise claim clearly named MayCommit before entering a possibly noninterruptible owner commit. ACK facts are separate.",
